5-person plan for Meadow House Repairs
I’ve assumed the morning session (freeze 12:30, now about 10:46, so roughly 1h45 left). For the afternoon session, add 4 hours to every time.
Approach
Plain HTML + CSS + JavaScript, no framework, no install, with everything saved in localStorage. Each person owns one or two files and edits only those, so you won’t get merge conflicts.
File	Owner
index.html, app.js, README.md	Person 1
storage.js	Person 2
form.js	Person 3
render.js, styles.css	Person 4
workflow.js	Person 5
Load order in index.html: storage.js, render.js, form.js, workflow.js, app.js.
The contract (agree this by 10:58)
Person 1 pastes this into the repo as CONTRACT.md so nobody has to guess.
js
// Job shape
{
  id: "MH-0001",              // from a saved counter, never list length
  house: "Meadow House",
  description: "Garden fence damaged",
  reporter: "Alex Morgan",
  priority: "Urgent",         // "Normal" | "Urgent"
  status: "New",              // "New" | "In Progress" | "Completed"
  createdAt: "2026-10-19T10:50:00.000Z",
  history: [ { at: ISOString, status: "New", note: "Report created" } ]
}

// storage.js (Person 2)
loadJobs()                        -> array
createJob({description, reporter, priority}) -> job
addProgress(id, note)             -> job   // status becomes In Progress, adds history
completeJob(id, note)             -> job   // throws Error("...") if note is blank/spaces
getJob(id)                        -> job

// render.js (Person 4)
renderJobs()                      // redraws the whole list from loadJobs()
// each job card contains <div class="job-actions" data-job-id="MH-0001"></div>

// workflow.js (Person 5)
renderJobActions(job, container)  // fills that .job-actions div

// app.js (Person 1) - global helper everyone uses for feedback
announce(message, focusElement?)  // writes to the live region, optionally moves focus
Golden rules:
Show user text only with textContent, never innerHTML. This is how test 10 passes.
After any change, call renderJobs().
Use these exact button names everywhere: Submit report, Start work, Save progress note, Mark completed.
