Person 2: Storage and data (storage.js)
loadJobs() and a private saveJobs(), using localStorage with try/catch and a fallback of [].
nextId() using a separately saved counter, giving MH-0001, MH-0002 and so on. IDs must stay unique after a refresh.
createJob(): status New, house: "Meadow House", createdAt as an ISO timestamp, and a first history entry {at, status:"New", note:"Report created"}.
addProgress(id, note): set status to In Progress and push a history entry. Never remove or overwrite earlier entries. It should also work for a second note on a job that’s already In Progress.
completeJob(id, note): if note.trim() is empty, throw an error and change nothing. Otherwise set Completed and push a history entry.
Change only the job with the matching ID, so jobs stay independent (test 5).
Open the browser console and test it by hand. Push a working version by 11:15 so the others can plug in.
Afterwards, help Person 1 with the refresh test (test 9).
Person 3: Report form and validation (form.js)
Build the form inside #report-form:
Description (textarea) with a real <label>
Reporter name (input) with a real <label>
Priority (select or radio buttons: Normal / Urgent) with a label
