Person 4: Job list, detail, history and styling (render.js + styles.css)
Display (render.js)
renderJobs() clears #job-list and draws one card per job, newest first. Each card shows: ID, created date, Meadow House, description, reporter, priority in words (“Priority: Urgent”), status, and the latest note.
Show the full history on each card: date and time, status and note, with every entry kept in order.
Use textContent for everything user-typed and test with <b>check gate</b>.
Add an empty <div class="job-actions" data-job-id="..."> in each card, then call Person 5’s renderJobActions(job, container) for it (check that the function exists first, so your code still works before theirs is ready).
Show “No repairs reported yet.” when the list is empty.
Styling (styles.css)
6. No horizontal page scrolling at 1440×900 or 390×844. Use a single-column layout on mobile.
7. Body text and labels 14px or more (use 16px), helper text 12px or more.
8. Contrast at least 4.5:1, so dark text on light backgrounds. Show Urgent with the word plus a colour/badge, never colour alone.
9. A clear :focus-visible outline on every button, input, select and textarea.
10. overflow-wrap: anywhere on description and note text, so a 200-character entry stays readable.
11. Make buttons look different from plain text and keep their styling consistent.
Person 5: Progress and completion workflow (workflow.js)
Write renderJobActions(job, container) and call it fresh each time the list is redrawn.
Inside each job’s actions area, provide:
a Note textarea with a label (“Progress note for MH-0001”)
Start work and Save progress note buttons (a first progress note moves the job to In Progress; later notes keep it In Progress)
a Completion note input with a label, plus a Mark completed button
For a Completed job, hide or disable the forms and show the completion note clearly.
A blank or spaces-only progress note shows an error beside that field.
A blank or spaces-only completion note shows an error beside that field. Status, notes and history stay exactly as they were (test 7). Catch the error thrown by completeJob().
Link errors with aria-describedby and aria-invalid="true".
After success, call renderJobs() and then announce("Progress note saved for MH-0001") or announce("MH-0001 marked Completed").
Check that only the clicked job changes (test 5).
